## 3. Dynamic UX# Application Enhancements Walkthrough

## 3-Tier AI Fallback Engine (PDF Parser Resilience)
I have successfully overhauled the application's PDF extraction core to prevent AI Rate Limit failures.
### What Changed
1. **Persistent Central API Analytics**: Integrated an `ApiUsageCounter` directly into your PostgreSQL Prisma structure surviving Vercel cold restarts and Debian system flushes natively.
2. **Tier 1 (Google Gemini 2.0)**: Wired specifically to push raw base64 arrays skipping local extraction. Triggers automatically up to 1,400 hits daily.
3. **Tier 2 (Groq)**: Wired the OpenRouter replacement cleanly to `llama-3.3-70b-versatile` catching any HTTP 429 rate limit emissions cascaded from Tier 1. Operates on physical strings converted securely via `pdf-parse` running up to 14,000 hits daily.
5. **Provider UI Labels**: Re-compiled the generic Import Modals and underlying Server Actions (`/api/medicines/import`) to transmit secure `X-AI-Provider` headers, injecting `Processed by Google Gemini ✓`, `Processed by Groq ✓`, or `Processed by OpenRouter (slow mode) ✓` dynamically into the front end component trees.
6. **Client-Side OCR Overrides**: Intercepted the native [parseTextWithAI](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/lib/aiParser.ts#903-954) routing loop for Image uploads, converting the raw textual extraction from your browser's Tesseract directly into Gemini payloads before defaulting to the Slow OpenRouter cascade. This explicitly solves the Cloudflare HTTP 524 Timeout you encountered when picking the "Run OCR" option on bad PDFs.
## 3. Dynamic UX Flow Enhancements (Post-Deployment Additions)
* **Under 3-Month Expiry Guard:** We added an aggressive [isExpiringSoon()](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/components/AddInventoryModal.tsx#155-162) boundary checking logic on the frontend that immediately paints a yellow HTML warning alert (`⚠️ This batch expires soon - are you sure you want to add it?`) if the user attempts to ingest medications expiring within the next 90 days.
* **Intelligent MRP Hydration:** Selecting a medication triggers a silent background microservice hit (`/api/medicines/[id]/last-mrp`) resolving to the **most recent** [InventoryBatch](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/app/dashboard/inventory/page.tsx#22-34) ever committed for that medicine block, pre-filling the `MRP` value down to the cent instantly to significantly speed up continuous ingestion cycles.

## 4. Bulk CSV Integration & Master Accounting Exporters
* **Atomic Import Engine (5k Row Limit)**: Engineered a massive multi-dependency CSV router inside the "Bulk Import Data" Settings tab. The engine strictly forces HTML5 dates, positive integers, and validates payloads row-by-row. If **one** single dependency is malformed, the entire transaction reverts automatically guaranteeing unbreakable database relationships.
* **Intelligent Excel Reporting**: Live "Download Excel" reporting buttons were securely bolted directly above both the **Inventory** and **Returns** ledgers.
* **Temporal Sorting Logic**: The extracted Excel spreadsheets are piped out via `<Blob>` array buffering with real-time `EXPIRING SOON` or `EXPIRED` conditional coloring injected directly into the active strings. And, because you requested it, the entire grid drops out perfectly sorted by `Expiry Date (Ascending)` locking hazardous stock visually to the top!

